## 1 Initial Project Concept

### 1.1 Working Title

AI Companions

### 1.2 Current Concept

Describe what you currently imagine making, designing, researching, performing, or developing. Be as expansive as your current thinking requires; two to three sentences is the minimum. If you are not yet sure what your Culmination Project will be, describe the areas, practices, questions, technologies, or experiences you want to work within instead.

People are building deeply customized, persistent virtual entities with long-term memory that actively text them updates, remember obscure life details, and adapt their personalities over time. The concept of forging emotional bonds with a completely synthetic mind feels like something pulled straight out of a dystopian sci-fi novel, yet it's becoming an everyday reality for millions. It's an incredible leap in personalized engineering, but watching human social structures adapt to software that cares back—or at least simulates it convincingly—is wildly uncanny. Is the basis for what my culmination project can present.

### 1.3 Participant Experience

What might a participant, audience member, user, or collaborator see, hear, do, understand, or feel?

I interpret that any viewer observing my presentation on AI companions will intake information and absorb it, like any kind of person who sees interesting information.

### 1.4 Early Unknowns

List at least one important question, uncertainty, or problem that you need to investigate.

How can an AI companion maintain long-term, contextually accurate memory across massive user bases without incurring prohibitive computational costs or experiencing data degradation? What are the psychological impacts of users forming deep emotional attachments to synthetic entities, and where should developers draw the ethical line regarding simulated care?

