### 4.3 Project Type Response

After watching *Designing Your Culmination Project*, identify one or more project types that may fit your current idea. Explain why these possibilities fit, or why your project may be hybrid.

Write 2-4 sentences.

This project fits a hybrid category combining a software application/tool and an interactive digital media experience. It is a software tool because it relies on back-end data management, persistent memory architecture, and AI text-generation models to function. Simultaneously, it is an interactive digital media experience because its primary value lies in narrative dialogue, persona design, and shaping user psychology, emotional engagement, and social interaction.

### 4.4 Project Origin Response

How did you arrive at this project idea or area of interest, and why did you select it as a possible direction for your Culmination Project?

You may discuss personal experience, prior coursework, creative or technical interests, an existing project, a collaborator, or a possible CHI Meta-Project connection. Your answer may change as the project develops.

This project idea emerged from observing the rapid, surreal shift toward hyper-realistic AI companions that are fundamentally blurring the line between software and social interaction. I selected this as a possible direction for my Culmination Project because exploring the intersection of persistent memory architecture and synthetic empathy offers a compelling, cutting-edge space to investigate both advanced technical engineering and profound human-computer relationships.

